  "title": "Magnificat in D major",
  "composer": "J. S. Bach",
  "catalogue": "BWV 243",
  "description": "Bach composed his Magnificat in 1723, one of the first major works he produced after taking up his post as Thomaskantor in Leipzig. First performed at Christmas vespers at the Thomaskirche, it stands as a thrilling early statement of his ambitions in the role. Around a decade later Bach revised the work into the D major version performed today, scoring it for five-part chorus, soloists, and a festive orchestra with trumpets and timpani. Its twelve compact movements showcase his extraordinary range, moving from the blazing opening chorus through a sequence of intimate arias and duets to the thunderous fugal finale.",
